## Getting started with AWS

AWS- Amazon web services works on pay as you go model which means you will only pay if you are using the services
provide services in three model 1- IAAS 2-PAAS 3-SAAS

IAAS- Infrastructure  As a service
AWS provides network databses servser

PAAS- Platform as a service
AWS provides EC2,IAM,S3 etc

SAAS- Software as a service
examples are gmail google docs etc

EC2- Elastic compute cloud

EC2 is a vertual server provided by AWS which can be remotly acessed over the internet 

Horizontal Scaleing - Addding more server to handel traffic spike
Vertical scaleing - Adding more resourses to the same server

S3 is a simple storage service where we can store data as an object

IAM iddentity acess management 

it help to give user acess based on there role or adding the users into polices based on authentication authorisation

VPC Vertual private cloud

VPC allows us to create a vertual isolated network within the aws
componets are Public subnet,private subnet,NAT gateway,Internet gateway,routetabel
 
Public subnet-Exposed to internet via internet gateway
Private subnet- exposed to internet vai NAT which is placed in Public subnet
NAT Gateway- Network address tranlation is used to provide a sured internet to the pvt subnet
Internet gateway- Being used by Public subnet to connect to the internet 
Routetabel- used to route the tracfic to the subnect based on the rules.
